      "key": "room1",
      "title": "The dispatch cabin",
      "debrief": "Your first move was the analyst's first move: take the whole lake table and keep only the rows that clear a threshold. Counting the lakes above pH 8 is filter() — screen the many down to the few that meet a condition, and read off what is left.",
      "technique": "filter() — single condition, count/identify",
      "puzzleType": 1,
      "built": true,
      "authoring": {
        "tag": "room1",
        "scenePrompt": "This is a panorama. A 360-degree view from the centre of a rustic Alaskan search-and-rescue cabin at night, the room wrapping continuously all the way around so the left and right edges meet seamlessly. Ahead, a wooden desk with an open laptop showing a faint scatter-plot chart and a topographic lake map pinned on the log wall above it. To one side, a cork bulletin board crowded with pinned notes and photographs, and a single hand-written index card tucked into the frame beside it. Set into one wall, a small window fitted with a pane of deep red filtered glass that throws a warm crimson wash across that side of the cabin; beneath it a cast-iron stove, a steaming kettle and enamel mugs on a shelf. On the far wall, a heavy closed wooden door with a storm lantern hanging beside it. Around the rest of the cabin, log walls, shelves of field and camping gear, and the dark tundra beyond under a faint aurora. Warm lantern light and a crimson glass-glow against cool night, muted teal-and-amber palette with a red accent, drifting haze, film grain, richly detailed. No people, no lettering, no captions, no text.",
        "doorPrompt": "The heavy closed wooden door now stands wide open, revealing a dim interior passage leading deeper into the station toward the warm glow of a kitchen beyond; the crimson glass-glow across the cabin is unchanged. Identical lantern light, same painterly teal-and-amber style, no people, no lettering, no text."
      },
