          "body": "Getting your bearings: the data is <em>long format</em> — one row per lake per measured element — and per-lake readings like <code>water_temp</code> and <code>pH</code> repeat across that lake's rows, so count <em>distinct</em> lakes, not rows.<br><br>Here's what <code>str(alaska_lake_data)</code> shows — the shape of the data:<pre style=\"white-space:pre;overflow-x:auto;font:12px/1.45 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;background:#08131c;color:#cfe6d8;padding:8px 10px;border-radius:6px;margin:8px 0 0\">tibble [220 × 7] (S3: tbl_df/tbl/data.frame)\n $ lake        : chr [1:220] \"Devil_Mountain_Lake\" \"Devil_Mountain_Lake\" \"Devil_Mountain_Lake\" \"Devil_Mountain_Lake\" ...\n $ park        : chr [1:220] \"BELA\" \"BELA\" \"BELA\" \"BELA\" ...\n $ water_temp  : num [1:220] 6.46 6.46 6.46 6.46 ...\n $ pH          : num [1:220] 7.69 7.69 7.69 7.69 ...\n $ element     : chr [1:220] \"C\" \"N\" \"P\" \"Cl\" ...\n $ mg_per_L    : num [1:220] 3.4 0.028 0 10.35 ...\n $ element_type: chr [1:220] \"bound\" \"bound\" \"bound\" \"free\" ...</pre>\n\nAbbreviations:\n\nGAAR: Gates of the Arctic National Park & Preserve\nBELA: Bering Land Bridge National Preserve\nNOAT: Noatak National Preserve"
