      "debrief": "The way out was this entire lesson made physical. Each of Claire's three glass templates is a filter(): lay one over the tail-number board and it covers every number that fails its condition. Stack all three and exactly one tail number is still a clear window through every filter — the row that survives filter after filter after filter. That is why the escape was a code you could only read by filtering: filter(), filter(), filter(), and the one left standing is your answer.",
